                "Errors": [
                {
                    "Message": "gallery name not found",
                    "ErrCode": 5004
                }]
            }



# POST /gallery/remove_subject
####Removes a face you have enrolled within a gallery.

Pass in a gallery_name and a subject_id and we will remove that subject from the gallery.  Once the last subject is removed the gallery is removed automatically.

If the 'face_id' parameter is passed in the request, then the API will look for and only remove the individual enrolled template matching the corresponding 'face_id' but not all the matching subject_id's in the gallery.

+ Parameters
    + `subject_id`: `"subject_id":"Elizabeth"` (string, required) - Defined by you. `subject_id` is used as an identifier for the face.
    + `gallery_name`: `"gallery_name":"MyGallery"` (string, required) - Defined by you. `gallery_name` is used to identify the gallery.
    + `face_id`: `"face_id":"58f9034743ab64939482"` (string, optional) - A unique ID from the enroll output when an image has been enrolled.

<!--a class="apiarylink text-success bolder" target="_blank" href="https://kairos.docs.apiary.io/#reference/face-recognition/galleryremovesubject/post?console=1">Try it in our API sandbox</a-->

+ Request (application/json)
    + Headers

